      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So it really comes down to objective proof. What if the event is a series of small, seemingly unrelated incidents—like minor utility outages or supply chain hiccups—that happen almost in tandem? Could a tenant argue that these aggregate \"random\" disruptions constitute a force majeure event, or would the court just see that as an unlucky run of bad luck?",
